title: "Aiyagari (1994QJE): Uninsured Idiosyncratic Risk and Aggregate Saving - Computational Implementation"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
url: "https://github.com/econ-ark/Aiyagari1994QJE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/econ-ark/Aiyagari1994QJE"
abstract: >-
  This repository computes the stationary equilibrium of Aiyagari's (1994) economy,
  "Uninsured Idiosyncratic Risk and Aggregate Saving", for every cell of its Table II,
  with two toolkits: HARK's (Heterogeneous Agents Resources and toolKit)
  MarkovConsumerType, and dolo with DolARK, its extension to heterogeneous agents. Both
  solve Aiyagari's own economy, his seven-state Tauchen chain for income, and one code
  computes both toolkits' stationary populations, on a grid of its own. At converged
  settings the two agree to within a few thousandths of a percentage point; Aiyagari's
  published values differ from both by up to 0.26 percentage points. Results of record
  for each toolkit at each level of settings are in table-ii/. For the baseline
  calibration, the HARK notebook also draws the consumption functions, the wealth
  distribution and the supply of and demand for capital, and saves those figures and the
  economy's key numbers. The HARK computation is also a Python package, aiyagari1994qje,
  that other programs can install to compute the same numbers.
